From 7157000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RistOS Build <build@ristos.org>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] rist: point network location at the Rist relay (root pins kept)

Move NETWORK_LOCATION_GRAPHENEOS_APPLE_PROXY (setting value 2, the ONLY value
RistOS ever writes -- see NetworkLocationConsent.VALUE_PROXY) from GrapheneOS's
relay to ours:

    https://gs-loc.apple.grapheneos.org/clls/wloc   ->   https://loc.ristos.org/clls/wloc

Nothing else about the exchange changes. Same POST, same request bytes, same
four forwarded headers (Accept / Accept-Language / Content-Type /
User-Agent, all already set by fetch() above getServerUrl()), same 10 s connect
and 10 s read timeouts, and the response comes back byte-for-byte as Apple sent
it, so the "skip 10 bytes, protobuf-decode the rest" path in fetch() is
untouched. No authentication is added, deliberately: authenticating the device
would identify it, which is the whole thing this relay exists to prevent. No
X-Forwarded-For / Via / proxy header is added either.

Values 1 (NETWORK_LOCATION_APPLE) and 3 (NETWORK_LOCATION_APPLE_CHINA) are left
pointing at Apple. They are honest as they stand, they are not what RistOS
writes, and the Settings labels for them ("Apple server", "Apple China server")
stay true. Only the proxy row becomes ours.

Pins are ISRG roots only; never pin the leaf (Let's Encrypt rotates it).

============ SHIPS WITH ========================================================
This patch makes the Settings radio label "GrapheneOS Apple proxy" wrong. It
must land in the same image as aosp/rro/RistSettingsStrings, which renames that
one string to "Rist Apple proxy", and as the reworded prompt in
app/src/main/java/watch/rist/assistant/NetworkLocationPromptActivity.kt, whose
refusal screen tells the user to pick that exact label by name. Landing any one
of the three without the other two leaves an instruction on screen that names a
control the user cannot find.
---
 res/xml/network_security_config.xml                             | 13 ++++++++++++-
 .../app/grapheneos/networklocation/ApplePositioningService.kt   |  6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/res/xml/network_security_config.xml b/res/xml/network_security_config.xml
--- a/res/xml/network_security_config.xml
+++ b/res/xml/network_security_config.xml
@@ -2,8 +2,19 @@
 <network-security-config>
     <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false"/>
     <domain-config>
-        <domain includeSubdomains="true">gs-loc.apple.grapheneos.org</domain>
+        <domain includeSubdomains="true">loc.ristos.org</domain>
         <!-- no expiry since the app is expected to be kept relatively up-to-date to use the services -->
+        <!-- RistOS: these are ISRG *ROOT* pins, and they must stay that way. loc.ristos.org uses
+             Let's Encrypt with ~90-day auto-renewal, so pinning the leaf certificate or its
+             public key would break positioning on every shipped handset at the first renewal,
+             in the field, with no recovery path. The
+             served chain is loc.ristos.org -> Let's Encrypt YE2 -> ISRG Root YE -> ISRG Root X2
+             (cross-signed by ISRG Root X1), and the SHA-256 SPKI hashes of ISRG Root YE and
+             ISRG Root X2 in that chain match the two pins below byte for byte. The leaf's own
+             SPKI hash (SEIKiCw+Vid+afQQ79R5UDHUYL257SuG513uuIXAqfg=) is deliberately ABSENT.
+             Failure here is graceful (ApplePositioningService throws IOException and the
+             platform falls back to satellite positioning silently), but it would be a silent
+             field-wide accuracy regression, so do not narrow this set. -->
         <pin-set>
             <!-- ISRG Root X1 -->
             <pin digest="SHA-256">C5+lpZ7tcVwmwQIMcRtPbsQtWLABXhQzejna0wHFr8M=</pin>
diff --git a/src/app/grapheneos/networklocation/ApplePositioningService.kt b/src/app/grapheneos/networklocation/ApplePositioningService.kt
--- a/src/app/grapheneos/networklocation/ApplePositioningService.kt
+++ b/src/app/grapheneos/networklocation/ApplePositioningService.kt
@@ -97,7 +97,11 @@
             NETWORK_LOCATION_APPLE_CHINA ->
                 "https://gs-loc-cn.apple.com/clls/wloc"
             NETWORK_LOCATION_GRAPHENEOS_APPLE_PROXY ->
-                "https://gs-loc.apple.grapheneos.org/clls/wloc"
+                // RistOS: the same Apple endpoint, relayed by Rist instead of GrapheneOS. The
+                // request bytes, the response bytes and the 10-byte-skip decode are unchanged;
+                // only the host that forwards them differs. Pinning for this host lives in
+                // res/xml/network_security_config.xml -- ISRG ROOTS ONLY, never the leaf.
+                "https://loc.ristos.org/clls/wloc"
             NETWORK_LOCATION_APPLE ->
                 "https://gs-loc.apple.com/clls/wloc"
             NETWORK_LOCATION_DISABLED ->
--
2.43.0
